Package: rhizome-graph
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: any
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12),
 python3 (<< 3.13),
 python3-watchdog,
 python3-gi,
 gir1.2-webkit2-4.1,
 libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0
Recommends: git
Suggests: chromium | chromium-browser | google-chrome-stable, firefox
Description: real-time visualizer of what each Claude Code agent is doing
 rhizome-graph watches a project while one or more Claude Code agents work in
 it and draws the result as a live force-directed graph in the Gource idiom:
 one figure per agent, a beam to every file it adds, edits, deletes or reads.
 .
 Events arrive from two sources at once, because neither is enough alone. The
 PostToolUse hook carries the agent id, which is the only way a change can be
 credited to an actor, but it cannot resolve a glob or a compound shell
 command. The filesystem watcher sees every change on disk and knows no
 author. The daemon combines them, seeds the existing tree at boot, and serves
 the page and its event stream over one port.
 .
 The bounds on python3 are not decoration. This package carries a virtualenv
 holding one wheel, websockets, because the daemon imports
 websockets.asyncio.server and the version Debian ships predates that module;
 a virtualenv runs under the Python minor version it was built for and under
 no other. Everything else comes from the distribution.
 .
 git is recommended rather than required: without it the diff view and the
 uncommitted-changes panel stay quiet and the graph is untouched.
